{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793565246,"nonce":"nLDcfrwwH+/QblT8Ot5e6eX9uO0=","title":"@keyframes can't move gradient stops","message":"A keyframe's background gradient keeps only its first and last stop colours and its angle (blinc_css parser/keyframes.rs). Stop positions don't interpolate, so a highlight swept across an element by moving its stops, the usual skeleton shimmer, can't be written in CSS:\n\n    @keyframes shimmer {\n      from { background: linear-gradient(90deg, base -60%, shine -30%, base 0%); }\n      to   { background: linear-gradient(90deg, base 100%, shine 130%, base 160%); }\n    }\n\ncn::skeleton pulses its opacity meanwhile. Do: carry every stop (colour and position) through keyframe props and interpolate them, then move the skeleton to the sweep.\n\nashui first: components/css/components.css @keyframes ui-skeleton-shimmer and .ui-skeleton.","files":null}]}